mma 82a: 'shetehei ishah mashkemes ve'ofah').","note_he":"עזרא תיקן ״שתהא אשה משכמת ואופה״ כדי שתהא פת מצויה לעניים (בבא קמא פב ע״א)."},{"text":"Chagiras Sinar LaIshah","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["חגירת סינר לאשה","חגירת סינר לאישה","אשה חוגרת בסינר","chagirat sinar laishah","chagiras sinar laisha","wearing a sinar","women wearing an apron","a woman wearing a modesty apron","wearing an apron","apron","sinar","סינר","חגירת סינר","a woman should wear a sinar for modesty"]},{"text":"Chafifah Lifnei Tevilah","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["חפיפה לפני טבילה","חפיפה קודם טבילה","אשה חופפת וטובלת","chafifa lifnei tevila","chafifoh lifnei teviloh","hafifa lifnei tevila","hair washing before immersion","combing hair before immersion","washing and combing before mikveh","pre-mikveh hair preparation","chafifah","chafifa","חפיפה","חפיפת שיער לפני טבילה","preparing and combing hair before mikvah"]},{"text":"Rochlin Machazirin BaAyaros","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["רוכלין מחזירין בעיירות","רוכלים מחזרים בעיירות","rochelim mechazrim baayarot","rochlin machzirin baayaros","Rochlei HaTachshitim","peddlers circulating in towns","cosmetics peddlers in towns","allowing travelling cosmetics sellers","peddlers selling cosmetics","cosmetics sellers","peddlers","רוכלים","רוכלין","רוכלי בשמים","מוכרי תכשיטי נשים","travelling sellers of women's cosmetics"]},{"text":"Tevilas Baal Keri","tier":"familiar","aliases":["טבילת בעל קרי","טבילה לבעלי קריין","טבילת עזרא","tevilat baal keri","tevilas ezra","tevilat ezra","Ezra's immersion","immersion for a baal keri","baal keri immersion","immersion after a seminal emission","baal keri","בעל קרי","טבילה לבעל קרי","a baal keri immerses before learning Torah"]}]},{"id":"q6","prompt":"Name an activity restricted in a synagogue under Shulchan Aruch, Orach Chaim 151.","prompt_he":"ציינו פעולה המוגבלת בבית כנסת לפי שולחן ערוך, אורח חיים קנא.","category":"Halacha","question_type":"attribute_or_action","difficulty":"easy","provenance":"ai_draft","answers":[{"text":"Sechok","tier":"familiar","aliases":["שחוק","צחוק","צחוק של קלות ראש","sekhok","schok","laughter","laughing","frivolous laughter","frivolous laughing","laughing frivolously","laughing for amusement","recreational laughter"],"note":"OC 151:1 lists frivolous laughter as kalus rosh. This entry concerns levity, not every expression of happiness or a claim that all smiling is forbidden.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א נזכר שחוק כדוגמה לקלות ראש. הכוונה לשחוק של קלות ראש, ולא לקביעה שכל חיוך או ביטוי שמחה אסורים."},{"text":"Hitul","tier":"familiar","aliases":["היתול","התול","לעג","ליצנות","hittul","heetul","mockery","mocking","derision","taunting","sarcasm","scoffing","mocking people","making fun of someone","Leitzanus Shel Kalus Rosh","mocking other people"],"note":"OC 151:1 separately names hitul among forms of kalus rosh. Mockery and derision are grouped here rather than counted as several extra answers.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א היתול נזכר בנפרד כדוגמה לקלות ראש. לעג וליצנות נכללים כאן באותה תשובה, ולא נספרים כתשובות נוספות."},{"text":"Sichah Beteilah","tier":"surface","aliases":["שיחה בטלה","שיחה בטילה","שיחות בטלות","דיבורי סרק","פטפוטי סרק","sicha betela","sichah betelah","sichah betalah","sichat batala","sichas beteilah","idle conversation","idle talk","idle chatter","chatting idly","pointless chatter","unnecessary chatting","talking about nothing","chatting","idle chatting"],"note":"OC 151:1 restricts idle conversation. Do not read this as a blanket prohibition of Torah discussion, prayer, or every necessary communal conversation.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א נאסרה שיחה בטלה. אין הכוונה לאסור דברי תורה, תפילה או כל שיחה הנצרכת לענייני הציבור."},{"text":"Achilah","tier":"surface","aliases":["אכילה","לאכול","אכילה בבית הכנסת","achila","akhilah","akhila","achiloh","eating","eating food","having a meal","eating in shul","eating a meal","snacking","having a meal for personal pleasure"],"note":"OC 151:1 restricts eating, with a necessity allowance for scholars/students and a Rema qualification for a beis midrash. Section 4 also gives synagogue-need and specified mitzvah-need permissions; not every meal is categorically forbidden.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א נזכרים היתר לתלמידי חכמים ותלמידיהם מדוחק ודעת הרמ״א בבית מדרש. בסעיף ד יש גם היתרים לצורך בית הכנסת ולצורך מצווה המתואר שם; אין כאן איסור גורף על כל אכילה."},{"text":"Shetiyah","tier":"surface","aliases":["שתייה","שתיה","לשתות","שתיה בבית הכנסת","shetiya","shtiyah","shtiya","shesiyah","shesiya","shesiyoh","drinking","having a drink","drinking refreshments","drinking in shul","having a drink in shul"],"note":"OC 151:1 restricts drinking alongside eating, with the stated necessity allowance for scholars and students and the Rema's beis-midrash qualification. This is a conditional restriction, not a practical ruling on every drink.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א נאסרה שתייה לצד אכילה, עם ההיתר הנזכר לתלמידי חכמים ותלמידיהם מדוחק והסתייגות הרמ״א בבית מדרש. אין זו פסיקה מעשית גורפת על כל משקה."},{"text":"Kishut","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["קישוט","קשוט","להתקשט","התקשטות","kishoot","grooming","adorning oneself","personal adornment","beautifying oneself","grooming oneself","getting dressed up","personal grooming","personal beautification in shul"],"note":"OC 151:1 says not to adorn oneself there. This is personal grooming/adornment, not the cleaning and honoring of the synagogue encouraged elsewhere in this chapter.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א נאמר ״ולא מתקשטין בהם״. הכוונה להתקשטות אישית, ולא לניקוי בית הכנסת ולכיבודו הנזכרים בהמשך הסימן."},{"text":"Tiyul","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["טיול","לטייל","טיול לשם הנאה","tiyyul","tiul","Tiyul BeVeis HaKnesses","strolling","sauntering","leisurely strolling","strolling for pleasure","wandering for recreation","walking around for amusement","aimless strolling","using the shul for recreational walking"],"note":"OC 151:1 restricts strolling for recreation. Walking for prayer, learning, or another legitimate synagogue purpose is not this answer.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א נאמר ״ולא מטיילין בהם״. הליכה לצורך תפילה, לימוד או צורך ראוי אחר של בית הכנסת אינה בכלל הטיול הנדון כאן."},{"text":"Knisah Mipnei HaChamah VeHaGeshamim","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["כניסה מפני החמה והגשמים","כניסה מפני החמה","כניסה מפני הגשמים","מחסה מהגשם","מחסה מהשמש","כניסה רק למחסה","knisa mipnei hachama vehageshamim","knisah mipnei hachamah","knisah mipnei hageshamim","knisoh mipnei hachamoh","sheltering","taking shelter","entering for shelter","sheltering from rain","sheltering from the sun","escaping the heat","entering only to escape the rain","using shul as a shelter","entering solely for shade","taking shelter from sun or rain","going in only to stay out of the sun"],"note":"OC 151:1 forbids entering solely to escape heat or rain. The two weather cases form one answer; entry for prayer or study is not forbidden merely because it is raining or hot.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א נאסרה כניסה רק מפני החמה או הגשמים. שני המקרים מאוחדים לתשובה אחת; אין איסור להיכנס לתפילה או ללימוד רק מפני שמזג האוויר חם או גשום."},{"text":"Cheshbonos Shel Reshus","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["חשבונות של רשות","חישובים של רשות","חישוב חשבונות חול","חשבונות","חישובי כספים","cheshbonot shel reshut","cheshbonos","cheshbonot","financial calculations","secular accounts","doing accounts","doing financial accounts","calculating business accounts","business bookkeeping","bookkeeping","monetary calculations","public financial accounts","חשבונות של רבים","accounting","working on ordinary financial accounts"],"note":"OC 151:1 permits mitzvah accounts, such as charity and redeeming captives, but not ordinary accounts. Section 11 also names public accounts as a disgraceful use of a ruined synagogue; both cases share this entry.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א הותרו חשבונות של מצווה, כגון צדקה ופדיון שבויים, ולא חשבונות רגילים. בסעיף יא נזכרים גם חשבונות של רבים כתשמיש מגונה בחורבה; המקרים מאוחדים כאן."},{"text":"Hesped SheEino Shel Gadol HaIr","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["הספד שאינו של גדול העיר","הספד רגיל","הספד","הספדים","hesped","hespeid","eulogy","eulogies","eulogizing","delivering an ordinary eulogy","a private eulogy","ordinary eulogies","an ordinary eulogy","eulogizing an ordinary person"],"note":"OC 151:1 gives an exception for a eulogy for a prominent member of the city for whom the whole city gathers. Do not infer that every eulogy or every funeral in a synagogue is forbidden.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א הוחרג הספד לאחד מגדולי העיר שכל בני העיר מתקבצים להספידו. אין להסיק שכל הספד או כל הלוויה בבית הכנסת אסורים."},{"text":"Knisah Likro LeAdam","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["כניסה לקרוא לאדם","כניסה לקרוא למישהו","כניסה לצורך עצמו","כניסה לצורך פרטי בלבד","knisa likro leadam","knisoh likro leadam","knisah letzorekh atzmo","knisah letzorech atzmo","entering to call someone","entering to call someone out","entering for a personal errand","entering solely for personal needs","entering just to fetch someone","coming in only to summon a friend","entering only to get a friend"],"note":"OC 151:1 describes entering to call someone for a personal need: first read/learn a little, or follow the alternative prescribed there for someone unable to do so. The restriction is entry solely for the errand without that qualification.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, א מתוארת כניסה לקרוא לאדם לצורך פרטי: יש לקרוא או ללמוד מעט תחילה, או לנהוג בחלופה הנזכרת למי שאינו יודע. ההגבלה היא על כניסה לצורך הפרטי בלבד, ללא התנאי הנדרש."},{"text":"Sheinah","tier":"surface","aliases":["שינה","לישון","תנומה","שינת עראי","sheina","sheinoh","shenah","shena","sleeping","sleep","napping","nap","dozing","taking a nap","even a short nap","dozing off"],"note":"OC 151:3 restricts even casual sleep in a synagogue, distinguishing a beis midrash. Section 4 permits sleeping for synagogue needs and gives Yom Kippur night as an example; this is not an absolute ban in every circumstance.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, ג נאסרה בבית כנסת אף שינת עראי, בשונה מבית מדרש. בסעיף ד הותרה שינה לצורך בית הכנסת ונזכר ליל יום הכיפורים כדוגמה; אין זה איסור מוחלט בכל נסיבה."},{"text":"Kapandria","tier":"familiar","aliases":["קפנדריא","קפנדריה","קיצור דרך","קיצור הדרך","kapandriya","kapandarya","Kitzur HaDerekh","shortcut","shortcuts","short cut","taking a shortcut","using shul as a shortcut","cutting through the synagogue","entering one door to leave another as a shortcut","walking through to shorten a route","using the shul to shorten one's route"],"note":"OC 151:5 restricts entering to shorten one's route. It gives exceptions for an earlier public path, entry not initially intended as a shortcut, and entering to pray; leaving by another door is not inherently forbidden.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, ה נאסרה כניסה כדי לקצר את הדרך. נזכרים חריגים לדרך שקדמה לבית הכנסת, לכניסה שלא נועדה מתחילה לקיצור ולכניסה לתפילה; יציאה בפתח אחר אינה אסורה כשלעצמה."},{"text":"Knisah BeSakin Arukh","tier":"obscure","aliases":["כניסה בסכין ארוך","כניסה בסכין ארוכה","סכין ארוך","סכין ארוכה","knisa besakin arukh","knisah besakin aruch","knisoh besakin aruch","sakin arukh","sakin aruch","long knife","a long knife","bringing in a long knife","entering with a long knife","carrying a long knife into shul","bringing a long knife into shul"],"note":"OC 151:6 reports 'some prohibit' entering with a long knife. This entry preserves that attribution and the long-knife qualifier; it is not a blanket ruling about every small knife or modern weapon.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, ו נאמר ״ויש אוסרים״ להיכנס בסכין ארוך. יש לשמור על הייחוס לדעה זו ועל הגבלת הסכין הארוך, ולא להסיק איסור גורף על כל סכין קטנה או כלי נשק מודרני."},{"text":"Knisah BeRosh Meguleh","tier":"familiar","aliases":["כניסה בראש מגולה","בראש מגולה","ראש מגולה","בלי כיסוי ראש","knisa berosh meguleh","knisoh berosh meguleh","rosh meguleh","berosh meguleh","b'rosh meguleh","bareheaded entry","entering bareheaded","an uncovered head","uncovered head","without a head covering","entering without a head covering","bareheaded","entering with one's head uncovered"],"note":"OC 151:6 cites an opinion forbidding entry bareheaded. This is the head-covering restriction as quoted there, not a statement that its application is identical for every man, woman, and child.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, ו מובאת דעה האוסרת כניסה בראש מגולה. זו ההגבלה המצוטטת שם, ולא קביעה שכל דיני כיסוי הראש חלים באותו אופן על כל איש, אישה וילד."},{"text":"Hasharas Rok Galuy","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["השארת רוק גלוי","רוק גלוי","רקיקה בלי שפשוף","רקיקה ללא כיסוי","hasharat rok galui","hashoras rok goluy","rok galuy","leaving spit visible","leaving spittle exposed","spitting without rubbing it away","spitting and leaving it uncovered","not rubbing away spit","unremoved spit","leaving saliva exposed on the floor","leaving spit uncovered on the floor"],"note":"OC 151:7 permits spitting if it is rubbed away or concealed in reeds so it is not visible. The restricted act here is leaving it exposed, not spitting under every circumstance.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, ז הותרה רקיקה אם משפשפים את הרוק או אם הוא נבלע בגמי ואינו נראה. המעשה המוגבל כאן הוא השארתו גלוי, ולא כל רקיקה באשר היא."},{"text":"Zeriah BeChurvas Beis HaKnesses","tier":"pearl","aliases":["זריעה בחורבת בית הכנסת","זריעה בחורבת בית כנסת","זריעה בבית כנסת חרב","זריעה","לזרוע","zeria bechurvat beit haknesset","zeriah bechurvat beit haknesset","zeria bechurvas beis haknesses","zeriah","zeria","zeriyah","planting","sowing","planting crops","sowing crops","planting in a ruined synagogue","growing crops in a ruined shul","using a synagogue ruin for planting","planting crops where a shul used to stand"],"note":"OC 151:11 explicitly lists planting as a disgraceful use forbidden even in a ruined synagogue. A building-time stipulation permitting ordinary use after destruction does not permit this degrading use.","note_he":"באורח חיים קנא, יא זריעה נזכרת במפורש כתשמיש מגונה האסור אף בחורבת בית כנסת. גם תנאי שנעשה בשעת הבנייה ומתיר שימוש רגיל לאחר החורבן אינו מתיר תשמיש מגונה זה."}]},{"id":"q7","prompt":"Name a Chief Rabbi of the United Hebrew Congregations of the Commonwealth or its London predecessor office from 1704.","prompt_he":"ציינו מי שכיהן כרב הראשי של הקהילות העבריות המאוחדות של חבר העמים, או במשרת הרבנות הלונדונית שקדמה לה משנת 1704.","category":"Wildcard","question_type":"person_by_role","difficulty":"easy","provenance":"ai_draft","answers":[{"text":"Aharon Hart","tier":"obscure","aliases":["אהרן הארט","אהרון הארט","אהרן הרט","אהרון הרט","Aaron Hart","Rabbi Aaron Hart","Aaron Uri Phoebus Hart","Aharon Uri Feibush Hart","אהרן אורי פייבוש הארט"]},{"text":"Tzvi Hirsch Levin","tier":"pearl","aliases":["צבי הירש לוין","צבי הירש לוויין","הירשל לוין","הרט ליון","הרץ ליון","Tzvi Hirsh Levin","Zvi Hirsch Levin","Zvi Hirsh Levin","Hirschel Levin","Hirschell Levin","Hirsch Levin","Hart Lyon","Hart Lion","Hirschel Lewin","Hirschel Lowenstamm","Hirschel Lowenstam","Hirschel Berliner","Levin","Lewin","Lyon"],"note":"Known in England as Hart Lyon, he led London's Great Synagogue in 1758-1764 and was recognized by the Hambro congregation. His son later served as Chief Rabbi Solomon Hirschell. Source: Office of the Chief Rabbi, History of the Chief Rabbinate.","note_he":"רבי צבי הירש לוין, שנודע באנגליה כהרט ליון, כיהן ברבנות בית הכנסת הגדול בלונדון בשנים 1758-1764 והוכר גם בידי קהילת המבורו. בנו היה הרב הראשי שלמה הירשל. מקור: תולדות הרבנות הראשית באתר לשכת הרב הראשי."},{"text":"David Tevele Schiff","tier":"obscure","aliases":["דוד טבלי שיף","דוד טבל שיף","דוד טעבלי שיף","דוד טעבל שיף","David Tevele Shiff","David Tevel Schiff","David Tebele Schiff","David Tewele Schiff","Tevele Schiff","Tevel Schiff","Schiff","Shiff","שיף"]},{"text":"Shlomo Hirschell","tier":"obscure","aliases":["שלמה הירשל","שלמה הירשעל","שלמה הירש","Shlomo Hirschel","Shelomo Hirschell","Solomon Hirschell","Solomon Herschell","Solomon Hirschel","Solomon Hirsch","Hirschell","Herschell","הירשל","הירשעל"]},{"text":"Nasan Marcus Adler","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["נתן מרקוס אדלר","נתן אדלר","Nathan Marcus Adler","Nathan Adler","Natan Marcus Adler","Nosson Marcus Adler","Nosson Adler","Nasan Adler","Nathan M Adler","נתן מרקוס הכהן אדלר"]},{"text":"Naftali Tzvi Hirsch Adler","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["נפתלי צבי הירש אדלר","נפתלי אדלר","הרמן אדלר","נפתלי הרמן אדלר","Naftali Adler","Naftali Zvi Hirsch Adler","Hermann Adler","Herman Adler","Hermann Adler HaKohen","Naftali Hermann Adler"]},{"text":"Yosef Tzvi Hertz","tier":"familiar","aliases":["יוסף צבי הרץ","יוסף הרץ","הרץ","Yosef Zvi Hertz","Yosef Hertz","Joseph Herman Hertz","Joseph Hertz","Joseph H Hertz","J H Hertz","Hertz","Rabbi Hertz"]},{"text":"Yisrael Brodie","tier":"uncommon","aliases":["ישראל ברודי","ברודי","Israel Brodie","Yisroel Brodie","Yisrael Brody","Israel Brody","Isidor Brodie","Brodie","Brody","Sir Israel Brodie"]},{"text":"Immanuel Jakobovits","tier":"familiar","aliases":["עמנואל יעקובוביץ","עמנואל יעקובוביצ","יעקובוביץ","Immanuel Jacobovits","Immanuel Jacobowitz","Immanuel Jakobovitz","Emmanuel Jakobovits","Emmanuel Jacobovits","Jakobovits","Jacobovits","Jacobowitz","Jakobovitz","Lord Jakobovits","Rabbi Jakobovits"]},{"text":"Yaakov Tzvi Sacks","tier":"surface","aliases":["יעקב צבי זקס","יעקב צבי זאקס","יונתן זקס","יונתן סאקס","זקס","זאקס","Jonathan Sacks","Jonathan Henry Sacks","Jonathan H Sacks","Jonathon Sacks","Rabbi Sacks","Lord Sacks","Lord Jonathan Sacks","Sacks","Sachs","Yaakov Zvi Sacks","Yaakov Tzvi Sachs","Jacob Zvi Sacks"]},{"text":"Efrayim Mirvis","tier":"surface","aliases":["אפרים מירוויס","אפרים מירביס","אפרים מרוויס","מירוויס","מירביס","Ephraim Mirvis","Efraim Mirvis","Ephrayim Mirvis","Rabbi Mirvis","Mirvis","Sir Ephraim Mirvis"]}]}]}
